{"descriptionModels":[{"description":"Prerequisites: You must have received a dragon blessing or enhacement from an Young or older Dragon (The dragon must also be a True Dragon, either Chromatic, Gem, Metallic or other) either by favor, the energy released upon it\u0027s death or bathing or drinking portions of it\u0027s blood.\n\nYou gain some of the majestic presence of a dragon. You gain the following:\n\nDragon\u0027s Speech: You can speak, read, and write Draconic. You have advantage in Charisma checks to influence creatures of the Dragon type that can understand your speech.\n\nDragon\u0027s Voice: You know and can cast the Thaumaturgy cantrip. When you do so, you can choose a target of your choice that can hear you. That target has disadvantage in the next Wisdom saving throw it makes.\n\nDragon’s Wiles: As a bonus action, you can give yourself a bonus to your next Charisma (Persuasion, Deception or Intimidation) check equal to your proficiency bonus, even if you already do.","level":1}],"id":"Custom1fa552d4-bcf6-498b-817f-399d5503cda6","isFeature":false,"jsonType":"feat","level":1,"name":"Draconic Gift of Presence [FTD] [SM]","notes":"","type":"Feat"}